Ladybird skips building the event path only for a trusted event that
nothing on the path listens for, so an untrusted event always leaves
its target set after dispatch. Each engine sets the target whether or
not any listener runs: WebKit’s EventDispatcher::dispatchEvent()
builds its EventPath and skips only dispatchEventInDOM() when
listenerCounts has none, then sets the target to the last context’s
target; Blink’s EventDispatcher::DispatchEventPostProcess() sets it
to the window event context’s target; and Gecko’s EventDispatcher::
Dispatch() sets mTarget before building its chain, and clears it only
when ShouldClearTargets() says to.
